  "revised": "2026-11-10",
  "firmware": "1.02 r1",
  "source": "Treetech AVR Mapa de Protocolos de Comunicação MAP-103, rev. 1.00",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "AVR - Relé Regulador de Tensão: Mapa de Protocolos de Comunicação (MAP-103)",
      "version": "1.00",
      "date": "2025-08-18",
      "url": "https://treetech.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Treetech_AVR_v2_mapa_de_protocolo_pt_1.00.pdf",
      "note": "section 2 (Modbus); linked in issue #153"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS-485, FC01 to FC06, FC15 and FC16. Addresses are 0-based, as sent on the wire.",
    "Baud rate is selectable (4800 to 115200 bit/s), 8 data bits, no parity, 1 or 2 stop bits (detected automatically). The document gives no factory default for the baud rate or the address; 9600 and 1 are assumed here.",
    "The document lists every value as a 16-bit word without stating a scale. Scales are applied where the documented range makes them clear (frequency, angles, power factor, VT voltage) or where the TMV / SDV / SDT document (MAP-013) lists the same register with an engineering range; those descriptions say so. The line current stays raw.",
    "Left out: the regulation sets (registers 20100 to 20620 and coils 20100 to 20601), the relay-to-alarm association coils, the password and mass-memory registers, the 48-bit timestamp, the tap changer rated current (21305, whose range differs from the TMV document) and the squared-current limits in 21404 to 21408.",
    "The document was written for firmware 1.02 r1. Written from that document; this map has not been tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "parity": "N",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
